# {{name}}

A background worker on [id_effect](https://github.com/Industrial/id_effect), generated by `id-effect new --template worker`.

```sh
cargo test     # six virtual hours of jobs in milliseconds
cargo run      # runs the jobs on the system clock; Ctrl-C stops them (exit 130)
```

## Jobs

`src/lib.rs` declares them in one `CronRegistry`:

| Job | Schedule | Policy |
|---|---|---|
| `heartbeat` | `* * * * *` (every minute) | an overlapping fire time is skipped |
| `cleanup` | `0 3 * * *` (03:00 UTC) | a missed night is caught up once |

Each fire time is recorded in the scheduler's run history (`scheduler.history("cleanup")`: fire time, start, end, outcome; the last 100 per job), and the `on_success` / `on_failure` hooks print finished runs. Give an expression a time zone with `Cron::parse(..)?.in_zone(..)` (DST-aware).

`main.rs` hands the jobs to `run_main`: the first Ctrl-C interrupts them, in-flight runs stop and the process exits `130`.

## Run it elsewhere

- `docker compose up --build` — the image from `Dockerfile`.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — fmt, clippy, test and a docker build on every push.
